cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use prophound, please cite it as below."
title: "prophound: a recall-first, database-free prophage screen for prokaryotic genomes"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jacob
    family-names: Alford
    email: jalford0000@gmail.com
  - given-names: Benjamin
    family-names: Alford
    email: ssolar5.dev@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SyrinxInformatics/mge-detect"
abstract: >-
  prophound localizes candidate integrated prophages directly from nucleotide
  sequence, with no gene calling or reference database at run time. A
  reverse-complement-symmetric CNN, trained on geNomad-labelled genomes, scores
  sliding 10 kb windows as an ensemble of three training replicates, and calls
  are built from the score track. It is tuned to recover already-known elements
  and returns everything else as candidates for follow-up, at a cost in calls
  per genome the user sets with one of three modes.
keywords:
  - prophage
  - bacteriophage
  - mobile genetic elements
  - deep learning
  - metagenomics
